From 26fbed6ddbeff271635913619ee3fc90b1a94093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thibaut <thibaut-leaux-angeli@live.fr>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:08:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/33] d3d12_xs: device slot 133 (CreatePlacedResourceX) makes
 a buffer on the title's own pages

Xbox device slot 133 is (va, desc, state, clear, riid, out): the title places a buffer at the VA of a
physical-page range it has just mapped (docs/retail_boot_chain.md 3.4, #6915). The proxy now hands it to
a handler the Vulkan layer registers (set_placed_at_va_handler), which imports [va, va + width) with
VK_EXT_external_memory_host and binds a VkBuffer to it: the CPU's writes there are the GPU's reads with no
copy, and the resource's console VA is the title's VA, so views and immediate writes the title names by
that VA resolve to it through the buffer VA index. The Xbox flag bits above the PC ones are dropped and
the layout made ROW_MAJOR, as slot 76 does; textures are E_NOTIMPL, a misaligned VA E_INVALIDARG, and
with no handler (a PC device) the slot refuses with E_NOTIMPL as #6953's table does.

Not decided here: a shader that adds heap_base to the title's VA (its own V#s) does not reach these
pages; that needs the single address space of docs/d3d12_vulkan.md 3.3.

d3d12_existing_heap_test: on a VirtualAlloc range and on a view of a pagefile-backed section (the form
xmem's physical pages take), the buffer's GPU VA is the address and a GPU copy to a READBACK buffer reads
a pattern the CPU wrote after creation; Vulkan validation clean on an RTX 4090.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
